<title>USA: Seitel Participates in Successful Gas Discovery.</title>
<headline>Seitel Participates in Successful Gas Discovery.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seitel Inc said it has a 33.33 percent working-interest in the LL&amp;E Fee No. 1, a natural gas discovery in south Louisiana made by Louisiana Land and Exploration Co.</p>
<p>The well, located at West Paradis in St. Charles Parish, La., flowed at four million cubic feet of natural gas and 74 barrels of condensate per day on a 14/64-inch choke with flowing tubing pressure of 3,853 pounds per square inch, during a recent production test, LLX said earlier.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
